    explain: 'Step-by-Step Geometric Mensuration Solution:\n1. Area of the Square Garden = side² = 21 m × 21 m = 441 m².\n2. Four Corner Quarter-Circle Flower Beds (radius r = 7 m):\n   Combined Area = 4 × (1/4 × π × r²) = π × 7² = (22/7) × 49 = 154 m².\n3. Semicircle Beds on each of the 4 Sides:\n   Along each 21 m boundary side, two 7 m corner beds leave a straight segment in the middle:\n   Remaining length = 21 − (7 + 7) = 7 m.\n   The straight edge of each semicircle is 7 m (Diameter = 7 m, radius r_semi = 3.5 m = 7/2 m).\n   Combined Area of 4 Semicircles = 4 × (1/2 × π × (7/2)²) = 2 × (22/7) × (49/4) = 77 m².\n4. Total Bed Area = Corner Beds (154 m²) + Side Beds (77 m²) = 231 m².\n5. Area of Shaded Lawn = Total Square Area − Total Bed Area = 441 m² − 231 m² = 210 m².',
    source: '01_AM2_Aptitude_Mock_Test_2.pdf (Q20)',
