    answer: 0,
    explain: 'Alphabetical Positional Shift Rule:\nAnalyze the forward shift for each consecutive character of \'BUILD\':\n• B (2) + 2 = D (4)\n• U (21) + 3 = X (24)\n• I (9) + 4 = M (13)\n• L (12) + 5 = Q (17)\n• D (4) + 6 = J (10)\nThe rule increments the shift by +1 for each letter: (+2, +3, +4, +5, +6, +7...).\nNow apply this rule to \'CREATE\':\n• C (3) + 2 = E (5)\n• R (18) + 3 = U (21)\n• E (5) + 4 = I (9)\n• A (1) + 5 = F (6)\n• T (20) + 6 = Z (26)\n• E (5) + 7 = L (12)\nResulting Word = E - U - I - F - Z - L = EUIFZL (Option A).',
